(5779204, 840595, 10785, '<td valign="top">The Post Processing gives this a really cool film look. It does have a very yellowish color cast. The high contrast and enhanced sharpening of the photo makes it loose a little of that loving feeling. I enjoy the Depth of Field which is spot on!</td>', 'The Post Processing gives this a really cool film look. It does have a very yellowish color cast. The high contrast and enhanced sharpening of the photo makes it loose a little of that loving feeling. I enjoy the Depth of Field which is spot on!', '2009-12-23 11:09:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5779212, 841271, 10785, '<td valign="top">A great capture of a couple who have weathered the years together. Obvious love is portrayed here. I would suggest you kick this up a notch by moving the subjects to a more condusive setting for portraits rather than leaving them on the couch. Try near a window or something. The busy background kind of detracts</td>', 'A great capture of a couple who have weathered the years together. Obvious love is portrayed here. I would suggest you kick this up a notch by moving the subjects to a more condusive setting for portraits rather than leaving them on the couch. Try near a window or something. The busy background kind of detracts', '2009-12-23 11:12:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5779217, 841046, 10785, '<td valign="top">Excellent lighting and set up. Good Depth of field. You are in John 3, but due to the position of the subject on the page and the shallow DoF you can''t really see verse 16 pertaining to God''s love. You can see the verse about the money changers clearly where he made a scourge to drive them out of the temple, but that speaks more to the Wrath of God than his love. Try repositioning this so that the greatest love verse of all is apparent. Or you can try other great love verses in the bible, such as in 1 Corinthians 13 among others.</td>', 'Excellent lighting and set up. Good Depth of field. You are in John 3, but due to the position of the subject on the page and the shallow DoF you can''t really see verse 16 pertaining to God''s love. You can see the verse about the money changers clearly where he made a scourge to drive them out of the temple, but that speaks more to the Wrath of God than his love. Try repositioning this so that the greatest love verse of all is apparent. Or you can try other great love verses in the bible, such as in 1 Corinthians 13 among others.', '2009-12-23 11:20:37.000000', NULL, 1),
