(5787032, 841248, 30982, '<td valign="top">If I look at this on my really too light monitor (I have an old one I use for text stuff) I can see what looks like artifacting in the upper two-thirds (the darker part) from something like shadows/highlights or Topaz.  On my normal monitor it is not visible, but I can see where it would be on some laptops depending on the angle viewed.  I suppose the way you can check is to turn the brightness up on your monitor, but then you''d have to worry about it being too dark on other monitors... just go with what looks good to you!</td>', 'If I look at this on my really too light monitor (I have an old one I use for text stuff) I can see what looks like artifacting in the upper two-thirds (the darker part) from something like shadows/highlights or Topaz.  On my normal monitor it is not visible, but I can see where it would be on some laptops depending on the angle viewed.  I suppose the way you can check is to turn the brightness up on your monitor, but then you''d have to worry about it being too dark on other monitors... just go with what looks good to you!', '2009-12-30 11:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
